			"date": "2025-06-06T22:30:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Nintendo did a talk at an AWS conference a couple years back where they went into some of the stack!<br> <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/ko/awstv/watch/34fbecfb62e/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">aws.amazon.com/ko/awstv/watch/</span><span class=\"invisible\">34fbecfb62e/</span></a></p><p>The WebKit/JIT part is from personal experimentation and I can't find a reliable third-party source unfortunately. I used to do Switch dev at a prev employer before switching (haha) to frontend, the same browser applet can be called generically from a game, so I spent a lot of time poking at it. Quite a few Switch games use it for in-game manuals actually!!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
